    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰν-ωλεθρία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>utter destruction</i>; by
			early writers used in dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανωλεθρίῃ ἀπολόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.120
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανωλεθρίᾳ δὴ </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ λεγόμενον</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> . . ἀπώλετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.87
				</span></i>
			: later in gen., <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				56.4
			</span></i>: nom. pl., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1049b
			</span></i>.</div>
